# Text checks out with LF on every OS. Git for Windows checks text out with CRLF by default
# (core.autocrlf=true), and the tests compare checked-out files with LF patterns and goldens.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Windows batch files (gradlew.bat) check out with CRLF on every OS, after `git add --renormalize`
# too. text stays auto, unlike Gradle's `text eol=crlf`, so the CRLF copy committed before this rule
# is not reported as modified.
*.bat eol=crlf
# Binary: never converted.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jar binary
